the latest research on school start  times and school performance shows that  if you change the school start time from  one that begins really early for example  seven o'clock to one which is much more  in tune with the child circadian rhythm  grades go up and the children do better  and and this is something that I think  people need to be aware of there have  been actual states where they have  changed the school start time for the  whole state this is happening for  example in Minnesota in some states  people are sort of chipping away at this  issue school system by school system but  in general it's much much better if the  child is able to start school at a time  when they are wide awake and alert  otherwise there daydreaming they're  asleep they're not performing as well as  they can I had a visit with a school  superintendent of one of the school  systems in Connecticut because I had a  patient that specifically had a problem  of not being able to handle waking up  five thirty in the morning in order to  finally start of their school classes at  7am and it was and you know and I was  met with sort of like why is this a  problem of the child waking up so early  in it and it hasn't quite entered  everybody sort of thinking yet that that  the children need to sleep the right  amount and they need to get up at a much  more reasonable time I can tell you that  I moved here from from Canada where the  school start time was almost nine  o'clock in the morning and and we didn't  have this problem of dragging children  out of bed in order to start school and  I'd love to see that here in Connecticut  parents need to recognize that their  child's performance is going to is going  to impart depend on how much sleep that  child gets and how alert they are and so  sleep needs to be made a priority and in  other words if a child needs 10 hours of  sleep at a given age they need to get 10  hours of sleep and the parent is going  to have to be hard-nosed about it if the  bus schedules is inflexible and can't be  changed so they're going to have to be  hard-nosed about it and just lay  lay down the rules and because otherwise  what will happen is the child will not  achieve the grades they can achieve and  that'll have a huge effect on them for  the rest of their life and a lot of  people don't realize that that that  doing poorly in school or failing even  one year is something that's going to  follow them for a big part of their life  you
 

